<title>JAPAN: Japan rice harvest estimated slightly down.</title>
<headline>Japan rice harvest estimated slightly down.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's rice harvest for this year was estimated at 10.316 million tonnes as of October 15, down by 408,000 tonnes from last year, the Agriculture Ministry said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Growth in northern Japan was slightly off due to insufficient sunshine and slightly low temperatures in July, the ministry said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>It also said planted acreage this year totalled 1.967 million hectares, down 139,000 hectares from last year.</p>
<p>The ministry said it would announce a final estimate of the rice harvest in mid-December.</p>
</text>
